 result←{object}∆WI action;Application;objname;objref;args;name;⎕TRAP;GUIroot;nametesting;resume;top
⍝ Entry point of DeltaWI package -- emulates APL+Plus ⎕WI system function

 ⎕TRAP←(870 'C' '⎕DM⊃⍛⎕SIGNAL ⎕EN')(888 'S')((0 1000)'C'ErrorSignal)    ⍝ Report all errors directly back to the application
 Application←⊃⎕THIS,⍨⎕THIS~⍨⎕RSI/⍨⎕THIS⍕⍛{(⊂⍺)≢¨⍵↑¨⍨≢⍺}⎕NSI             ⍝ Global: Where are we being called from (outside DeltaWI)?
 :If 0=⎕NC'#.⍙WI' ⋄ CreateRoot'#.⍙WI' ⋄ :EndIf                          ⍝ On our first call, create a root from which everything GUI grows
 GUIroot←#.⍙WI                                                          ⍝ Global: A master reference to our GUI structure root
 :If ×GUIroot ⎕VGET⊂'_Developer' 0 ⋄ ⎕TRAP[3]←⊂(0 1000)'S' ⋄ :EndIf     ⍝ But for developers, just stop immediately if errors happen

 :Hold '∆WI#',⍕⎕TID ⋄ top←1 ⋄ :Else ⋄ top←0 ⋄ :EndHold                  ⍝ Is this a recursive call? ⍝? This sequence could theoretically be interrupted by an in-thread event that might happen any time (high-priority??)
 top,⍨←0/⍨top∧'⎕Send'≡⊃⊆action                                          ⍝ Allow a ⎕Send to execute even while another thread is using ∆WI!   ⍝? Add ∆dlt here if Normalize does
 :Hold top/'∆WI'('∆WI#',⍕⎕TID)                                          ⍝ Make sure we stay single-threaded!

     ⍝ *** Pre-process the ∆WI call
     nametesting←⎕NULL∊action                                           ⍝ Allow for name-parsing-only internal testing to be performed
     :If 0=⎕NC'object' ⋄ object←⊢ ⋄ :EndIf                              ⍝ Allow monadic use
     (objname objref action)←object ObjectName action                   ⍝ Parse out object name to which this call applies
     :If nametesting ⋄ result←objname ⋄ :Return ⋄ :EndIf                ⍝ Allow for name-parsing-only internal testing to be performed
     :If resume←action≡,⊂,'*'                                           ⍝ Resume from within onAction handler?
         :Hold '∆WI@onAction' ⋄ resume←0 ⋄ :Else ⋄ resume←1 ⋄ :EndHold  ⍝ Are we really in the middle of onAction processing that can be continued?
     :AndIf resume                                                      ⍝ Are we still only resuming (only if we're on :Hold)
         action←Application ⎕VGET⊂'∆WARG'⍬                              ⍝ Reconstitute the original command and pass it back into onAction for resumption
     :EndIf
     (name args)←Normalize action                                       ⍝ Separate action name from its arguments and standardize top-level structure
     name←objref Canonize name                                          ⍝ In cases where capitalization is optional, adjust it to standard
     :If ⎕NULL≢result←objref(name Immediate)args ⋄ :Return ⋄ :EndIf     ⍝ Perform any out-of-band "instant" processing
     :If ⎕NULL≢result←objref((1↑action)OnAction resume)args ⋄ :Return ⋄ :EndIf  ⍝ Perform any application-specified alternative onAction processing

     ⍝ *** Time to execute the requested operation
     ⍝ Handle object creation cases separately using the .New namespace; otherwise start up the normal action processing by class
     :Select name
     :Case 'Create' ⋄ result←objref(LeafName objname)New.Create args    ⍝ Delete any existing GUI object and then recreate it
     :Case 'New' ⋄ result←objref(LeafName objname)New.New args          ⍝ Create a new GUI object as a child of its parent objref
     :Else ⋄ result←objref(name Invoke)args                             ⍝ Call the standard processing routine (by proxy), passing standard arguments
     :EndSelect

 :EndHold
